#, fuzzy
msgid "Settings"
msgstr "Ustawienia"

msgid "*The six tabs of the Settings dialog, section by section.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Settings dialog holds the choices that belong to this computer and to"
" you, not to a study: the language of the interface, the theme, your "
"identity, the nodes you know, the viewers, the AI provider and the add-"
"ons. A study carries its own texts, colours and vocabularies with it; the"
" settings stay on the machine."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the dialog with **Settings…** (:kbd:`⌘,` on macOS, :kbd:`Ctrl+,` on "
"Windows and Linux). On the macOS desktop the command is in the "
"**EMStudio** menu of the system's menu bar; on the web, on Windows and on"
" Linux it is in the **Help** menu."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dialog has six tabs: **General**, **Identity**, **Connections**, "
"**Viewers**, **Advanced** and **Add-ons**. The dialog reopens on the tab "
"you last used. Some commands open it directly on the section they need: "
"asking the narrative for a draft before an AI is set up opens **AI "
"provider**, an author's **Edit** opens **Identity**. **Save** applies the"
" changes, **Cancel** leaves everything as it was."
msgstr ""

msgid "General"
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "Language"
msgstr "Język"

msgid ""
"The language of this interface. Node labels and narrative text are "
"separate: they travel with the document, not with the app. EMStudio "
"starts in English and keeps the language you choose. For a language whose"
" translation is an AI draft, the option **I have read this translation — "
"mark it validated** turns off the “AI draft” badge on this computer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Settings, the General tab: language, texts of the graph, theme, Matrix "
"layout and interaction."
msgstr ""

msgid "Texts of the graph"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Show the texts in** sets the language the texts of the graph are shown "
"in, where the study holds a translation of them."
msgstr ""

msgid "Theme"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Auto (follows the system)**, **Light** or **Dark**. The theme changes "
"the interface and the canvas."
msgstr ""

msgid "Matrix · layout"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**«Layout» respects where I drop the nodes**: a node dropped by hand "
"keeps its place beside the nearest node at the next **Layout**. With the "
"option off, a drop moves the node by the same amount in the stored layout"
" too."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "Interaction"
msgstr "Interakcja"

msgid ""
"**Show connector tooltip on hover** is on by default. **Over a node of "
"the Chain: who, when, licence** shows three lines over a node of the "
"transformation chain; it is off by default, to try. **Strict document "
"naming (D.n)** is recommended: a document is called D.1, D.10 and so on. "
"The two **Photo lot** fields set when photographs of one camera, close in"
" time, are proposed as one lot: a new session after a number of minutes, "
"and at least a number of photographs. The lot is always confirmed by "
"whoever uploads."
msgstr ""

msgid "Files on this computer"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A study may name files in a OneDrive folder in a form that holds on every"
" computer. **OneDrive folder** says where OneDrive is on this one; **Find"
" it** looks for it. Until it is set, those files are marked as files to "
"link."
msgstr ""

msgid "Identity"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Settings, the Identity tab: the ORCID iD, name and surname, with Declare "
"and Verify with ORCID."
msgstr ""

msgid "Identity (ORCID)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ORCID iD is the identity: what you create and change carries the "
"signature of the current author. Write the **ORCID iD**, and if you wish "
"a **Name** and a **Surname**, then choose **Declare** to work at once, "
"offline. **Verify with ORCID** confirms the identity with ORCID; "
"verifying it is what unlocks publishing as that person. **Sign out · "
"forget this identity** removes it from this computer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The closed **Advanced** box holds the **ORCID client id (public)** and "
"the choice between orcid.org and its sandbox. These concern whoever "
"deploys EMStudio. Left empty, the desktop application uses EMStudio's own"
" client on orcid.org; a sandbox, or a web installation, needs a client of"
" its own, registered with its page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Connections"
msgstr ""

msgid "StratiGraph nodes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The nodes this computer knows. Each saved node can be made the "
"**default**, edited, tested and removed. **Add a node…** opens the node "
"selector, where you write a node's address and test it: EMStudio says "
"whether the address answers, whether it is a StratiGraph node, which "
"version it runs and which ways of signing in it offers. You choose a "
"node, sign in and pick its rooms from the chip at the top right of the "
"window."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Settings, the Connections tab: the StratiGraph nodes and the synchronised"
" apps."
msgstr ""

msgid "Orphan assets"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This section appears only to the operator of a node. It lists the files "
"of the node's store that no room cites any more, because their room was "
"deleted. They stay in the store, so the same file uploaded again is "
"stored once and joins its new room. The operator can filter them by type "
"and date, and delete them one at a time."
msgstr ""

msgid "Synchronised apps"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The live link with a tool on this machine or on your network. The chosen "
"tool is the host and EMStudio connects to it. **Sync with** offers "
"**Blender · EMtools** (the live link with EM Tools); the other entries "
"are marked *soon* and cannot be chosen. **Protocol** (local or secure), "
"**Host / IP** and **Port** compose the **Address** shown underneath."
msgstr ""

msgid "Viewers"
msgstr ""

msgid "3D viewer"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Where the 3D lives: the address of an **ATON server** and the path of the"
" **Heriverse app** under it. The **Scene** line shows the address that "
"results."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Settings, the Viewers tab: the ATON server, the Heriverse app and the "
"thresholds of big 3D assets."
msgstr ""

msgid "Big 3D assets"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The limits of EMStudio's own 3D viewer. A whole file or point cloud over "
"the **Threshold for a whole file (MB)** or the **Threshold for a whole "
"cloud (points)** does not load by itself: the viewer asks, and proposes "
"the tileset when the model has one. The **Tileset memory ceiling (MB)** "
"defaults to an eighth of this machine's memory; the tiles' textures are "
"reduced to fit it. **Tileset error set automatically** follows this "
"machine's profile; unticked, every tileset refines to the error chosen "
"with the slider, and each tileset's bar can still choose its own. The "
"**Scene memory ceiling (MB)** is set against the estimated weight of each"
" model before it is loaded: what does not fit is not loaded, and the "
"scene proposes the version that fits, or asks. The **Tile cache on disk "
"(MB)** keeps the tiles already seen on this machine, so that a tileset "
"does not come again over the network; 0 turns it off, and **Empty the "
"tile cache** clears it."
msgstr ""

msgid "3D navigation (the Space)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As in Blender: middle button to orbit, Shift + middle to pan, Ctrl + "
"middle to zoom. **Emulate 3 button mouse** makes Alt + left drag the "
"middle button. **Emulate numpad** makes the digits 1 3 7 5 0 of the top "
"row act as the keypad's. **Auto Perspective** makes an aligned view "
"orthographic, and orbiting returns to perspective. **Invert the "
"trackpad's orbit** turns the scene against the drag of two fingers. "
"**Left drag in the 3D** chooses what a left drag does: **Automatic** "
"(orbit, until a middle button is used), **Orbit**, **Box selection, as in"
" Blender**, or **Pan**. On macOS, choose **Pan** to pan with the three-"
"finger drag of the Accessibility settings. A line underneath says whether"
" a middle button has been used on this device."
msgstr ""

msgid "Images (IIIF)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The address of an IIIF Image API service (Cantaloupe, in the StratiGraph "
"stack). An image's identifier is its checksum, so only the host goes "
"here. Left empty, the images show without thumbnails from the service."
msgstr ""

msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Settings, the Advanced tab: the AI provider, the developer option and the"
" experimental functions."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "AI provider"
msgstr "Dostawca AI"

msgid ""
"Who writes the narrative drafts. **Provider** offers **Claude "
"(Anthropic)** and **Echo — local trial, no key**, which writes a fixed "
"draft and needs no network. **Model** may stay empty for the provider's "
"default. The **API key** is pasted and saved with **Save key**, and "
"**Remove** deletes it. The field stays empty after saving: the key can be"
" replaced or removed, and it is never shown again."
msgstr ""

msgid "Desktop"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The key goes into the system keychain and is passed to EMStudio's local "
"service, which restarts to receive it. While a draft is being written, "
"saving waits for it to finish."
msgstr ""

msgid "Web"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The key applies to the session only: it lives in the memory of EMStudio's"
" bridge while the bridge runs, and is not saved. The field works while "
"the bridge answers."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "Developer"
msgstr "Programowanie"

msgid ""
"**Show node UUIDs (inspector)** shows each node's identifier in the "
"Inspector. It is off by default."
msgstr ""

msgid "Experimental functions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Turn on the experimental functions on this machine** opens functions "
"still being tried. It is off by default and takes effect after a reload."
msgstr ""

msgid "Add-ons"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Settings, the Add-ons tab: this machine, the queue, and the tools "
"EMStudio downloads on request."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Tools EMStudio calls and does not ship. Each is downloaded on request "
"from its official releases, at a pinned version whose checksum is "
"verified. The tab shows this machine (system, processor, graphics, "
"memory), and for each tool its licence, source and version, and whether "
"it is **recommended**, **optional**, **not needed** or **not for this "
"machine** for what you do. The tools are:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**gltfpack**, which makes the light variants of a model in Ottimizza;"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Obj2Tiles**, which turns a textured mesh into a 3D Tiles tileset;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**3d-tiles-validator**, which checks every tileset against the "
"specification before it enters the graph;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Node.js**, EMStudio's own copy for the validator, needed only on a "
"machine without Node.js of its own."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each tool can be installed, updated and removed here. The tools that do "
"not run on this machine are listed apart, each with the reason. The add-"
"ons live in a folder of their own, outside the installer, and each keeps "
"its own licence."
msgstr ""

#, python-format
msgid ""
"**The queue: how much of this computer** chooses how many of these tools "
"work side by side: **All** runs several at once under a ceiling (the "
"performance cores less one, 60 % of the memory), **Half** uses half of "
"both, and **One at a time** runs them in turn."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The last card is **Blender**. It is not an add-on that EMStudio "
"downloads: it is the Blender of this machine, with its own add-ons (EM "
"Tools, 3D Survey Collection). EMStudio calls it in the background and "
"leaves it as it is."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The add-ons are managed by EMStudio's bridge: when the bridge does not "
"answer, the tab says so."
msgstr ""

